1
00:00:02,127 --> 00:00:03,587
"He sprang
to his sleigh

2
00:00:03,629 --> 00:00:05,255
"To his team
gave a whistle

3
00:00:05,297 --> 00:00:08,383
"And away they all flew
like the down of a thistle.

4
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:11,512
"But I heard him exclaim
ere he drove out of sight

5
00:00:11,553 --> 00:00:16,892
'Merry Christmas to all,
and to all a good night!'"

6
00:00:18,644 --> 00:00:22,439
Wow! That was great!

7
00:00:22,481 --> 00:00:24,107
You really wrote that?

8
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:26,986
Uh-huh.

9
00:00:27,026 --> 00:00:29,029
Say good-bye, elves,
I'm off to Tulsa.

10
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:32,157
Oh, I can't believe
you're not going to
be here for Christmas.

11
00:00:32,199 --> 00:00:33,742
You're really not coming back?

12
00:00:33,784 --> 00:00:35,369
Yeah.
We have all this paperwork

13
00:00:35,410 --> 00:00:38,038
that needs to be filed
by the end of the year.

14
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:39,874
If I don't get it done, 
I'll be fired.

15
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,041
Just, it's so unfair.

16
00:00:41,082 --> 00:00:42,543
You don't even like your job.

17
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:43,961
So, who does?

18
00:00:44,003 --> 00:00:45,420
Oh, I like my job.
I love my job.

19
00:00:45,462 --> 00:00:46,839
I can't wait
to go back to work.

20
00:00:46,881 --> 00:00:48,883
I can't get enough dinosaurs.

21
00:00:53,094 --> 00:00:55,347
I'm sorry I won't be here.

22
00:00:55,389 --> 00:00:58,225
It's hard enough
not seeing you
during the week

23
00:00:58,266 --> 00:00:59,852
but for Christmas...

24
00:00:59,894 --> 00:01:02,813
But if this is what you
have to do, I understand.

25
00:01:02,855 --> 00:01:05,357
Thanks.

26
00:01:05,399 --> 00:01:06,859
I'll see you New Year's Day.

27
00:01:06,901 --> 00:01:09,152
You're not going to be
here New Year's Eve?!

28
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:11,864
Did I not mention that?

29
00:01:11,906 --> 00:01:13,365
No.

30
00:01:13,407 --> 00:01:15,784
And to all a good night!

31
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:28,087
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

32
00:01:28,129 --> 00:01:30,465
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

33
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:32,968
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

34
00:01:33,010 --> 00:01:37,848
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

35
00:01:37,890 --> 00:01:39,850
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

36
00:01:39,892 --> 00:01:42,436
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

37
00:01:42,477 --> 00:01:46,523
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

38
00:01:46,565 --> 00:01:48,943
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

39
00:01:48,984 --> 00:01:51,445
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

40
00:01:51,486 --> 00:01:53,948
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

41
00:01:53,989 --> 00:01:56,450
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

42
00:01:56,491 --> 00:02:02,330
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

43
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:11,381
All right, everybody

44
00:02:11,423 --> 00:02:13,258
I know that it is
Christmas Eve

45
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:15,052
and you'd rather be
with your families.

46
00:02:15,094 --> 00:02:16,595
But there is no call

47
00:02:16,637 --> 00:02:18,639
for writing
"Screw You, Mr. Bing"

48
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:21,558
on the back of my chair.

49
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:24,352
By the way, you can
all call me Chandler.

50
00:02:25,604 --> 00:02:26,605
Hey.

51
00:02:26,647 --> 00:02:28,649
Hey, where've you been?

52
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:30,651
Oh, I was checking out
that insurance company's

53
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:31,902
Christmas party on three.

54
00:02:31,944 --> 00:02:33,445
I mean, it was really beautiful.

55
00:02:33,487 --> 00:02:35,489
They have all these decorations
and this huge tree

56
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:38,158
and I just thought, "To hell
with them, we have to work."

57
00:02:38,199 --> 00:02:40,869
So I stole their ham.

58
00:02:40,911 --> 00:02:42,871
You hear that?

59
00:02:42,913 --> 00:02:44,414
You may not be
with your families

60
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:46,917
but at least it's going
to smell like ham in here.

61
00:02:48,002 --> 00:02:50,253
My kid's in a play right now.

62
00:02:50,295 --> 00:02:53,298
You know what, I know
what will cheer you guys up.

63
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:55,759
Had a little talk with the boys
in New York

64
00:02:55,801 --> 00:02:57,845
told them about all
the hard work you've been doing

65
00:02:57,886 --> 00:03:01,056
and that a little
Christmas bonus may be in order.

66
00:03:01,098 --> 00:03:02,891
"A donation has been
made in your name

67
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:06,854
to the New York City Ballet."

68
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:10,774
Well, that's like money
in your pocket.

69
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:14,695
All right, look,
you want me to say it?

70
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:17,322
This sucks. Being here sucks.
This work sucks!

71
00:03:17,364 --> 00:03:19,825
Now it feels like Christmas.

72
00:03:19,867 --> 00:03:22,119
I'm sorry.

73
00:03:22,161 --> 00:03:23,996
Hey, at least you guys
get to go home

74
00:03:24,038 --> 00:03:25,622
and be with
your families tonight.

75
00:03:25,664 --> 00:03:27,457
I have to go back
to an empty hotel room

76
00:03:27,499 --> 00:03:31,837
and lay down on
a very questionable bedspread.

77
00:03:31,879 --> 00:03:33,505
And then tomorrow morning

78
00:03:33,547 --> 00:03:35,382
you get to have Christmas
morning in your own houses

79
00:03:35,423 --> 00:03:37,634
which by the way,
none of you have invited me to.

80
00:03:37,676 --> 00:03:38,886
You can come to my house.

81
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:41,513
( chuckles ):
No, thanks.

82
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:45,308
That's a nice pep talk.

83
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:47,061
Oh, thanks.

84
00:03:47,102 --> 00:03:50,064
I'm actually thinking about
becoming a motivational speaker.

85
00:03:50,105 --> 00:03:54,151
So, if you were home right now,
what would you be doing?

86
00:03:54,193 --> 00:03:56,111
Typical Christmas Eve stuff,
you know.

87
00:03:56,153 --> 00:03:58,030
Our holidays
are pretty traditional.

88
00:03:58,072 --> 00:04:02,076
Um, so here's a very
special holiday song

89
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:05,579
that I wrote for some very
important people to me.

90
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:08,540
( guitar strums )

91
00:04:08,582 --> 00:04:12,419
♪ Went to the store,
sat on Santa's lap ♪

92
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:15,797
♪ Asked him to bring my friends
all kinds of crap ♪

93
00:04:17,132 --> 00:04:20,635
♪ Santa, all you need
is to write them a song ♪

94
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:25,473
♪ They haven't heard it yet,
so don't try to sing along ♪

95
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:27,017
♪ No, don't sing along ♪

96
00:04:27,059 --> 00:04:28,518
( guitar playing )

97
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:34,649
♪ Monica, Monica,
have a happy Hanukkah ♪

98
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:43,951
♪ Saw Santa Claus,
he said hello to Ross ♪

99
00:04:43,992 --> 00:04:51,583
♪ And please tell Joey,
Christmas will be snowy! ♪

100
00:04:51,625 --> 00:04:59,674
♪ And Rachel and Chandler,
how's the... handler? ♪

101
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:01,093
Happy holidays, everybody.

102
00:05:01,135 --> 00:05:02,803
( applause )

103
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:04,387
Okay, Pheebs,
you look in the kitchen

104
00:05:04,429 --> 00:05:05,973
I will look in
the back closet, okay?

105
00:05:06,014 --> 00:05:07,141
I can save you
time, ladies.

106
00:05:07,182 --> 00:05:09,350
I'm right here.

107
00:05:09,392 --> 00:05:10,644
Yeah.

108
00:05:10,685 --> 00:05:12,229
Chandler, why don't you
take a walk.

109
00:05:12,271 --> 00:05:14,273
This doesn't concern you.

110
00:05:14,313 --> 00:05:16,524
We are looking for
our Christmas presents

111
00:05:16,566 --> 00:05:17,692
from Monica.

112
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,360
What? That's terrible.

113
00:05:19,402 --> 00:05:21,196
No, no, we do it
every year.

114
00:05:21,238 --> 00:05:23,865
Oh, well, that-that
makes it not terrible.

115
00:05:23,907 --> 00:05:26,868
No. Yeah, we never find them.

116
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:31,039
She's always bested us,
that wily... minx.

117
00:05:31,081 --> 00:05:32,457
Yeah, don't worry.

118
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:34,209
We're just going to search here
for an hour

119
00:05:34,251 --> 00:05:36,795
and then we're going to go over
to Joey's and search, okay?

120
00:05:36,837 --> 00:05:37,963
No, not okay.

121
00:05:38,005 --> 00:05:39,380
You can't look
for Monica's presents.

122
00:05:39,422 --> 00:05:40,381
Oh, no, we have to.

123
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:41,675
No, you don't have to.

124
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:45,344
And you can't
because I-I live here, too.

125
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:48,598
Well, then,
you should look with us.

126
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,309
Why?

127
00:05:50,349 --> 00:05:51,726
Chandler,
aren't you worried

128
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:53,145
about what to get
Monica for Christmas?

129
00:05:53,187 --> 00:05:55,563
No, I have a great idea
for a present for her.

130
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:58,817
Oh, that's it?
"A great idea." Oh, yeah.

131
00:05:58,859 --> 00:06:00,152
Chandler,
that's not enough.

132
00:06:00,194 --> 00:06:01,862
What if she gets
you a great present

133
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:04,323
two medium presents, and
a bunch of little presents

134
00:06:04,363 --> 00:06:06,491
and you've just gotten
her one great present?

135
00:06:06,533 --> 00:06:08,743
I mean, that's just going
to make her feel bad.

136
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:11,163
Why would you do that to
her, Chandler? Why? Why?

137
00:06:11,205 --> 00:06:13,915
If I help,
we could find them faster!

138
00:06:13,957 --> 00:06:15,292
That's right.

139
00:06:16,501 --> 00:06:17,669
Ooh!

140
00:06:17,711 --> 00:06:18,920
Ooh, we have a live one.

141
00:06:18,962 --> 00:06:20,297
Oh! It's a Macy's bag!

142
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:22,007
Yeah.

143
00:06:22,049 --> 00:06:23,091
Oh!

144
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:25,927
Ooh, who's it for?

145
00:06:25,969 --> 00:06:28,847
"Dear losers,
do you really think

146
00:06:28,889 --> 00:06:31,308
I'd hide presents
under the couch?"

147
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:35,312
"P.S. Chandler, I knew
they'd break you."

148
00:06:37,856 --> 00:06:40,441
Rach, these are for you.

149
00:06:40,483 --> 00:06:43,570
Wiper blades.

150
00:06:43,611 --> 00:06:45,404
I don't even have a car.

151
00:06:45,446 --> 00:06:49,743
No, but with
this new car smell,
you'll think you do.

152
00:06:52,371 --> 00:06:55,749
Okay, Pheebs,
your turn.

153
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:58,293
Oh!

154
00:06:58,335 --> 00:07:00,503
Toilet seat covers!

155
00:07:03,422 --> 00:07:06,218
Is that what you were doing
while I was getting gas?
Uh-huh.

156
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:08,345
You guys...

157
00:07:08,387 --> 00:07:10,513
JOEY:
Okay, and for Ross

158
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:12,515
Mr. Sweet Tooth...

159
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:18,188
You got me a cola drink?

160
00:07:18,230 --> 00:07:21,191
And... a lemon lime!

161
00:07:22,192 --> 00:07:25,362
Well... well, this...
this is too much.

162
00:07:25,404 --> 00:07:28,073
I feel like I should get
you another sweater.

163
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:33,287
And last,
but not least...

164
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:37,207
They're ribbed
for your pleasure.

165
00:07:38,499 --> 00:07:41,586
Hey, Ben

166
00:07:41,628 --> 00:07:43,671
what if the
Holiday Armadillo

167
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:47,342
told you all about
the Festival of Lights?

168
00:07:47,384 --> 00:07:49,010
Cool!
Right.

169
00:07:49,052 --> 00:07:50,387
Come on, Ben.

170
00:07:53,432 --> 00:07:55,850
Years and years ago

171
00:07:55,892 --> 00:08:00,147
there were these people
called the Maccabees!

172
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:04,151
Ho, ho, ho!
Merry Christmas!

173
00:08:05,526 --> 00:08:06,903
Santa!

174
00:08:06,945 --> 00:08:08,280
Hey!

175
00:08:08,322 --> 00:08:12,075
What are you
doing here, Santa?

176
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:16,871
Well, I'm here to see
my old buddy Ben.

177
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:23,211
What are you doing here,
weird... turtle... man?

178
00:08:23,253 --> 00:08:27,424
I'm the Holiday
Armadillo

179
00:08:27,466 --> 00:08:31,594
your part-Jewish
friend.

180
00:08:33,763 --> 00:08:36,766
You sent me here to give
Ben some presents.

181
00:08:36,808 --> 00:08:39,060
Remember?

182
00:08:39,102 --> 00:08:42,605
What?

183
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:44,774
Ben, why don't you come
open some more presents.

184
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:46,067
And Santa,
the Armadillo and I

185
00:08:46,109 --> 00:08:47,735
will have a little talk
in the kitchen.

186
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:50,613
There's a sentence
I'd never thought I'd say.

187
00:08:52,366 --> 00:08:54,242
What are you doing?!

188
00:08:54,284 --> 00:08:55,660
You called everyone and said

189
00:08:55,702 --> 00:08:57,912
you were having trouble
finding a Santa costume.

190
00:08:57,954 --> 00:09:00,332
So I borrowed one
from a guy at work.

191
00:09:00,374 --> 00:09:03,043
Thank you, but-but...
you got to leave.

192
00:09:03,084 --> 00:09:04,711
Why?

193
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:07,422
Because I'm finally getting him
excited about Hanukkah

194
00:09:07,464 --> 00:09:09,299
and then you're...
you're wrecking it.

195
00:09:09,341 --> 00:09:11,092
But I didn't get
to shake my belly

196
00:09:11,134 --> 00:09:13,594
like a bowl full of jelly.

197
00:09:16,555 --> 00:09:20,560
I'm sorry, Chandler, but this,
this is really important to me.

198
00:09:20,601 --> 00:09:24,647
Fine, I'll, I'll give
the suit back.

199
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:26,107
Hey...

200
00:09:26,149 --> 00:09:30,445
you think you can
keep it another night?

201
00:09:30,487 --> 00:09:33,198
Santa? Really?

202
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:35,158
Yeah, is that okay?

203
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:39,037
Did your Dad ever
dress up like Santa?

204
00:09:39,079 --> 00:09:40,788
No.

205
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:43,417
Then it's okay!

206
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:49,506
You know what?
Everybody, go home.

207
00:09:49,548 --> 00:09:51,132
You should be with
your families.

208
00:09:51,174 --> 00:09:53,343
It's bad enough that
we're working New Year's Eve.

209
00:09:55,554 --> 00:09:59,182
Did I not tell anyone
about New Year's Eve?

210
00:09:59,224 --> 00:10:01,642
Oh, all right, look, go.
Go home, okay.

211
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:02,727
Merry Christmas.

212
00:10:02,769 --> 00:10:04,312
Go.

213
00:10:04,354 --> 00:10:06,231
ALL:
Merry Christmas.
Peace on Earth.

214
00:10:06,273 --> 00:10:07,690
Bye.
Good.

215
00:10:07,732 --> 00:10:10,193
God speed,
good people.

216
00:10:11,528 --> 00:10:13,154
You're not going to go?

217
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:16,157
Nah. I couldn't
leave you alone.

218
00:10:16,199 --> 00:10:18,243
Ah, thanks.

219
00:10:18,285 --> 00:10:20,537
Besides, I can't leave

220
00:10:20,579 --> 00:10:22,663
until that Christmas party
downstairs clears out.

221
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:24,832
There are some pissed-off
insurance people

222
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:26,084
looking for that ham.

223
00:10:26,126 --> 00:10:28,044
Ah.
( telephone rings )

224
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:30,797
Chandler Bing.

225
00:10:30,838 --> 00:10:32,257
Hi, honey, we're all here.

226
00:10:32,299 --> 00:10:34,134
We just want to wish you
a Merry Christmas.

227
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:35,760
Merry Christmas!
Merry Christmas!

228
00:10:35,802 --> 00:10:38,472
Blah, blah!

229
00:10:38,513 --> 00:10:41,349
Oh, Merry Christmas.
I miss you guys.

230
00:10:41,391 --> 00:10:42,601
So is it horrible?

231
00:10:42,641 --> 00:10:44,102
Is everybody
working really hard?

232
00:10:44,144 --> 00:10:47,147
Ah, well, no.
It's just me and Wendy.

233
00:10:47,188 --> 00:10:50,066
Wendy?
That sounds like a girl's name.

234
00:10:50,108 --> 00:10:51,610
It is.

235
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:53,445
Did I not tell you about her?

236
00:10:53,487 --> 00:10:55,029
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm

237
00:10:55,071 --> 00:10:57,407
about the time you told me
about New Year's Eve.

238
00:10:57,449 --> 00:10:58,866
Where is everybody else?

239
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:00,368
I sent them home.

240
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:02,787
Oh, you are such
a good boss.

241
00:11:02,829 --> 00:11:04,705
Is she pretty?

242
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:07,208
Uh, uh...

243
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:09,586
Answer faster,
answer faster.

244
00:11:09,628 --> 00:11:10,629
I don't know.

245
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,631
Answer better,
answer better.

246
00:11:12,671 --> 00:11:15,049
I don't think of her that way,
you know.

247
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:16,759
She's a... she's a colleague.

248
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:18,052
What does she do there?

249
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:19,554
Oh, she's
Regional Vice President.

250
00:11:19,596 --> 00:11:21,055
She's just below me.

251
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:22,723
She did what?!

252
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:30,148
Be-low me.

253
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:34,152
Oh, wait, is Wendy
the runner-up Miss Oklahoma?

254
00:11:34,194 --> 00:11:35,694
What?

255
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:39,240
Well, sh-she didn't win.

256
00:11:39,282 --> 00:11:42,410
All right, well,
maybe I should let you

257
00:11:42,452 --> 00:11:45,580
and the second prettiest girl
in Oklahoma get back to work.

258
